From e92bd2d13f4acbf19c1a7d1cb2970061257da962 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:55:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] v4.8-gpu: clamp the task EMA climb at the budget
 ceiling

With the hardware-adaptive alpha at 4096 and FP_ONE at 256, a single
climb step can exceed the remaining gap to INFINITY_BUDGET_MAX_NS,
pushing the raw ema past the 6ms ceiling (observed at about 7ms for
briefly running tasks).  The weight math clamps the value downstream,
but the raw reading must stay within [0, BUDGET] so the per-process
stats and the EMA invariants hold; cap the step at the remaining gap.
The RT and group climbs cannot overshoot (alpha 4 and 1 respectively)
and are left unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
(cherry picked from commit 455ee87d9ec77b6075b70a679e3b2bc276843764)
---
 kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c b/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
index 615dbcd8d..9592bda0b 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
@@ -574,6 +574,15 @@ void infinity_consume(struct infinity_ctx *ctx, u64 delta_ns,
 	step = div64_u64((INFINITY_BUDGET_MAX_NS - ctx->ema) * delta_ns *
 			 alpha,
 			 INFINITY_BUDGET_MAX_NS * INFINITY_FP_ONE);
+	/*
+	 * With alpha up to 4096 (FP_ONE = 256) the step can exceed the
+	 * remaining gap to the ceiling, which would push ema past
+	 * INFINITY_BUDGET_MAX_NS (the weight math clamps it downstream,
+	 * but the raw value must stay within [0, BUDGET] so the
+	 * /proc/<pid>/infinity reading and the EMA invariants hold).
+	 */
+	if (step > INFINITY_BUDGET_MAX_NS - ctx->ema)
+		step = INFINITY_BUDGET_MAX_NS - ctx->ema;
 	ctx->ema += step;
 	atomic64_inc(this_cpu_ptr(&infinity_ema_climb_count));
 }
